#!/bin/bash
# ve-special-refuse — Git merge driver for TODO.md and project-facts.md
# Always refuse 3-way / auto text merge. Special-file protocol is mandatory
# every Master merge (against branch delta), not only when these paths change.

set -euo pipefail

# %O %A %B %L %P
P="${5:-special-file}"

cat >&2 <<EOF
ERROR: refusing git auto-merge of ${P} (text merge forbidden).

These files always require Master special-file review for THIS merge
(even if this path did not change on either side — review is driven by
what the branch did to the rest of the repo):

  TODO.md:
    - Start from master TODO (not the branch file).
    - todo-close items this branch implemented / PR or commits mark done.
    - todo-append only for genuine new future backlog (rare).
    - Never bulk-replace or naive-merge TODO.md.

  project-facts.md:
    - Start from master project-facts.
    - Prune/fix facts invalidated by this branch or post-fork reality.
    - Keep only stable orientation facts true after the merge.

Read: MASTER_AGENT_MANDATE.md §2 (Merge Strategy)
Skill: /master-merge  (.grok/skills/master-merge/SKILL.md)
Helper: ./merge-branch-into-master.sh <branch>

Keep ours (master), apply todo-append/todo-close and fact edits, then git add ${P}.
EOF

exit 1
